<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ginevra de' Benci</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1474–<a href="/years/1478">1478</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ginevra de' Benci is a portrait by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonardo-da-vinci">Leonardo da Vinci</a> of a young Florentine noblewoman, painted around 1474–1478. Long in the collection of the princes of Liechtenstein, it was sold in 1967 to the National Gallery of Art in Washington, the only painting by Leonardo in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ginevra-de-benci.jpg" alt="Ginevra de' Benci" width="320" height="339" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Leonardo da Vinci · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leonardo_da_Vinci_-_Ginevra_de%27_Benci_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
